§ `Independent tests — credit points under ss 33A, 34, 36 and 36A`

§§ `The persons in the independent tests`

-- Fields in the nouns module's order: resident in the tax year, woman,
-- Area resident who is not an Israeli citizen, foreign worker.

`independent: resident man` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`independent: resident woman` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`independent: non-resident man` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`independent: non-resident woman` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`independent: body of persons` MEANS `a body of persons`

`independent: Area non-citizen man` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`independent: Area non-citizen woman` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS TRUE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS FALSE)

`independent: foreign worker, resident man` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS TRUE)

`independent: foreign worker, resident woman` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS TRUE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS TRUE)

`independent: foreign worker, non-resident man` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS FALSE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS TRUE)

`independent: foreign worker, non-resident woman` MEANS `an individual` (Individual WITH
    `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                  IS FALSE
    `a woman`                                              IS TRUE
    `a resident of the Area who is not an Israeli citizen` IS FALSE
    `a foreign worker`                                     IS TRUE)

§§ `A — points per section per kind of person`

-- S01 resident man: s 34 "יחיד שהיה תושב ישראל בשנת המס ... שתי נקודות זיכוי"; s 36 "יחיד תושב ישראל ... 1⁄4"; s 36A "אשה" not met.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: resident man` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: resident man` EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident man` EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: resident man` EQUALS 9/4

-- S02 resident woman: as S01 plus s 36A "בחישוב המס של אשה תובא בחשבון 1⁄2". The s 134A(2) aggregate is ss 34 and 36 only.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: resident woman` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: resident woman` EQUALS 1/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: resident woman` EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident woman` EQUALS 11/4
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: resident woman` EQUALS 9/4

-- S03 non-resident man: "תושב ישראל" not met in ss 34, 36; not a woman.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: non-resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: non-resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: non-resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: non-resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: non-resident man` EQUALS 0

-- S04 non-resident woman: s 36A has no residence limb, only "אשה".
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: non-resident woman` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: non-resident woman` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: non-resident woman` EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: non-resident woman` EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: non-resident woman` EQUALS 0

-- S05/S06 body of persons (resident or not; the interface does not distinguish): not a "יחיד", not an "אשה".
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: body of persons` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: body of persons` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: body of persons` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: body of persons` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: body of persons` EQUALS 0

-- S07 resident man with no employment or travel: the interface asks nothing about work, which is the source's answer (s 36 body has no such limb).
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: resident man` EQUALS 1/4

-- S08 resident girl aged 16: no age limb in ss 34, 36, 36A; the interface asks no age, so she is the resident woman.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident woman` EQUALS 11/4

-- S10 Area resident, not an Israeli citizen, not an Israeli resident, man: ss 34/36 turn on an order under s 48; s 36A is 0 for a man.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: Area non-citizen man` BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: Area non-citizen man` BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: Area non-citizen man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: Area non-citizen man`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: Area non-citizen man`

-- S11 same, woman: s 48 does not name s 36A, and s 36A has no residence limb.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: Area non-citizen woman` BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: Area non-citizen woman` BECAUSE "section 48 and the order made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: Area non-citizen woman` EQUALS 1/2
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: Area non-citizen woman`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: Area non-citizen woman`

-- S12 foreign worker regarded as resident, man: s 48A "לא יחולו על עובד זר ... אף אם רואים אותו כתושב"; s 36A is 0 for a man whatever s 48A says.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: foreign worker, resident man` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: foreign worker, resident man` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: foreign worker, resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: foreign worker, resident man`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: foreign worker, resident man`

-- S13 foreign worker regarded as resident, woman: s 48A reaches every credit of the Chapter, s 36A included.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: foreign worker, resident woman` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: foreign worker, resident woman` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: foreign worker, resident woman` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: foreign worker, resident woman`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: foreign worker, resident woman`

-- S14 foreign worker, non-resident, man: ss 34/36 give 0 before s 48A, which can only take away.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: foreign worker, non-resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: foreign worker, non-resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: foreign worker, non-resident man` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: foreign worker, non-resident man` EQUALS 0

-- S15 foreign worker, non-resident, woman: ss 34/36 give 0; s 36A would give 1/2 and s 48A may take it away.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: foreign worker, non-resident woman` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: foreign worker, non-resident woman` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: foreign worker, non-resident woman` BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: foreign worker, non-resident woman`
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: foreign worker, non-resident woman` EQUALS 0

§§ `B — credit-point amounts (s 33A): points times the year's value, no rounding`

-- S21 resident man at V = 2,904: total 6,534; s 34 part 5,808; s 36 part 726.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident man` `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 6534
#ASSERT `the amount of` (`the credit points under section 34 for` `independent: resident man`) `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 5808
#ASSERT `the amount of` (`the credit points under section 36 for` `independent: resident man`) `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 726

-- S22 resident woman at V = 2,904: total 7,986; s 36A part 1,452.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident woman` `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 7986
#ASSERT `the amount of` (`the credit points under section 36A for` `independent: resident woman`) `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1452

-- S23 non-resident woman at V = 2,904.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: non-resident woman` `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 1452

-- S24 resident man at V = 2,903: 6,531.75 exactly; nothing in s 33A rounds.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident man` `at a credit-point value of` 2903 EQUALS 6531.75

-- S25 resident woman at V = 3,000.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident woman` `at a credit-point value of` 3000 EQUALS 8250

-- S26 body of persons at V = 2,904.
#ASSERT `the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: body of persons` `at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 0

-- S28 one credit point is the year's value: "נקודת זיכוי – סכום ... לשנת מס".
#ASSERT `the amount of` 1 `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 2904

-- S29 the statutory base sum: "סכום של 504 שקלים חדשים".
#ASSERT `the amount of a credit point as written in section 33A, before indexation` EQUALS 504

§§ `C — set-off against the tax: "המקוזז כנגד המס לאותה שנה"`

-- S30 resident man, V = 2,904, tax 20,000 → 13,466.
#ASSERT `the tax for the year after setting off` (`the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident man` `at a credit-point value of` 2904) `against` 20000 EQUALS 13466

-- S31 resident woman, V = 2,904, tax 5,000 → 0, never negative.
#ASSERT `the tax for the year after setting off` (`the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident woman` `at a credit-point value of` 2904) `against` 5000 EQUALS 0

-- S32 resident man, V = 2,904, tax 0 → 0.
#ASSERT `the tax for the year after setting off` (`the amount of the credit points under sections 34, 36 and 36A for` `independent: resident man` `at a credit-point value of` 2904) `against` 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `D — allowance point: the adjusted 1996 value "ומחולק בשנים עשר"`

-- S33, S34, S35 (A is my chosen input, not a published figure).
#ASSERT `the amount of an allowance point, given` 2904 EQUALS 242
#ASSERT `the amount of an allowance point, given` 2820 EQUALS 235
#ASSERT `the amount of an allowance point, given` 2905 EQUALS 2905/12

§§ `E — the aggregate s 134A(2) names: "נקודות הזיכוי שעל פי סעיפים 34 ו־36"`

-- S37 resident woman: 9/4 points (s 36A excluded) = 6,534 at V = 2,904; three times = 19,602.
#ASSERT `the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: resident woman` EQUALS 9/4
#ASSERT `the amount of` (`the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: resident woman`) `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2904 EQUALS 6534
#ASSERT 3 TIMES (`the amount of` (`the credit points under sections 34 and 36 for` `independent: resident woman`) `credit points at a credit-point value of` 2904) EQUALS 19602

§§ `F — tax-year edges`

-- S43 s 120B(e)(1): amounts are not adjusted on 1 January 2025-2027 and stay as on 1 January 2024.
-- Expressible only for the monthly booklet figures; the annual published figure refuses for 2024 and 2026.
#ASSERT `the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` 2025 EQUALS `the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` 2024
#ASSERT `the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` 2026 EQUALS `the monthly credit-point figure in the Israel Tax Authority's withholding booklet for tax year` 2024

-- ===========================================================================
-- NOT EXPRESSIBLE through the encoding's interface (see INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md):
--   S09a/S09b Israeli citizen resident in the Area (s 3A(f)): expected 9/4 and
--             11/4; no input distinguishes such a person from a non-resident.
--   S16       part-year resident: expected REFUSE; the residence input is a
--             BOOLEAN for the whole tax year.
--   S17       non-registered spouse married part of the year (s 41): expected
--             REFUSE; no marital input.
--   S18       woman inside her registered spouse's joint computation
--             (ss 65/66/38): expected REFUSE; no input.
--   S19, S20  sex or residence unknown: expected REFUSE; both are required
--             BOOLEANs (a required input is a legitimate handling).
--   S27, S36  value V or base A not supplied: both are required inputs
--             (legitimate).
--   S31       refund of an excess credit: not exposed.
--   S38-S42   tax years 2026, 2024, 1970, 1990, 1960: no rule takes a tax
--             year; the encoding answers for any year a caller supplies a V
--             for, and cannot refuse a year whose text the bundle lacks.
--   S43       annual published figures for 2024/2026/2027: refuse (no figure
--             sourced); only the monthly figures are comparable.
--   S44       kibbutz (s 57): only one kind of body of persons exists.
-- ===========================================================================
